�The Other Side Continent
The Other Side of the Continenta 20 years research that details sea voyages on the world's great oceans, including all those components that give light to an ancient effort to explore the Atlantic Ocean and probably even the American continent. The book includes 133 photographs, drawings, and watercolor paintings that illustrate historical and technical details about the seamanship of the ancient and medieval world."�

�
To proto best seller tromou apo Ellena suggraphea, e Nekre Gramme apotelei ena metaphusiko thriler pou kobei ten anasa kai anebazei ten agonia eos ten telike tou koruphose.
"Ora na anakalupsete auto to neo talento!"
-Nick Mamatas
"Ena exairetiko biblio. Sustenetai me to zori se kathe tromolagno kai suntagographeitai se opoiondepote agnoei e nomizei oti den uphistatai poiotiko Elleniko Phantastiko. Khreiazomaste perissotera tetoia biblia. Ta ekhoume apolute anagke."
-Mikhales Manolios
O Stamates Kokkinos skotose te gunaika tes zoes tou. E skepse aute ton basanizei kathe mera meta to trokhaio pou ten pere makria tou kai aphese piso ekeinon.
Oi meres tou kulane khoris noema mesa s' ena adeio diamerisma sto kentro tes Thessalonikes. Mone tou lutrose, ta teleutaia logia tes Ioannas ston telephonete tou.
Ostoso, ola osa pisteue o proen astunomikos tha anatrapoun otan gnorisei ton Ierokle, enan allokoto idiotiko ntetektib pou xerei gia ekeinon perissotera ap' osa tha 'prepe.
Mustika tou parelthontos pou arnountai na parameinoun thammena.
Amarties pou tha prepei na plerothoun me to megisto timema.
Kai ste mese olon, ena palio telephono pou khtupaei tis nukhtes, me phones nekron sten alle akre tes grammes.
Pou zetoun... ti;
Eirene, exileose, ekdikese...
Ena muthistorema pou sunduazei apsoga ten astunomike ploke me ton metaphusiko tromo!"�
�S aute te nea tou sulloge diegematon, eikosi pente kai parapano khronia meta ta tria klasika erga tou "Khoris Phtera", "Patsi" kai "Parenergeies", o Gounti Alen ekhei katapherei na mas dosei ena biblio pou okhi mono apanta sta pio bathia erotemata tes anthropines uparxes, alla ekhei kai to idaniko megethos gia na to baleis kato apo opoiodepote podi trapeziou pou palantzarei.
"Ksupnesa ten Paraskeue kai, epeide to sumpan diastelletai, mou pere perissotero apo to sunethismeno na bro te rompa mou>>, exegei se mia istoria gia ten episteme tes Phusikes, me titlo "Oi Oduneres Sunepeies tes Theorias ton Khordon". Se alla taxidia psukhobeltiotikes orthokrisias sunantame mia pleiada kharakteron, pou mono o Alen tha mporouse na phantastei: ton Tzasper Karudias, ton Phlanters Skoulek, ton megistana tes kinematographikes biomekhanias E. Koli Mpigks, gia na anapheroume mono ligous. Eite graphei gia tekhne, gia sex, gia phageto eite gia egklemata ("O Mpliakh einai astunomikos apo tote pou mporei na thumethei ton eauto tou. O pateras tou etan enas diaboetos lestes trapezon kai o monos tropos na pernaei o Mpliakh ligo khrono mazi tou etan na ton sullambanei"), to khioumor tou einai amimeto.
E "Skete Anarkhia" einai klasikos, protes taxeos Gounti Alen: dektikos, autosarkazomenos, etoimos gia mia ekrexe neurotikes uperboles, epheuretikos kai panexupnos. Dekaokhto xekardistika keimena, deka apo ta opoia demosieutekan arkhika sto New Yorker kai okhto pou kuklophoroun gia prote phora."�

�
Poor Bridgit, who overestimated the size of her head--her homemade frilly lace shower cap came straight down to her chin. And who can blame Lindsey for thinking "glitter shoes" sounded like a cool, easy project instead of what it turned out to be: a puddle of sparkling glop. And really, whoever posted that incredible Spaghetti-Stuffed Garlic Bread on Pinterest should be sued. When Mindy pulled hers from the oven, it looked like a "hot mess of intestines streaming out of doughy flesh." Mmmm, thank you, Pinterest!
Written by Heather Mann, publisher of CraftFail.com, her hilarious blog with millions of page views and hundreds of thousands of followers, CraftFailcelebrates the creative process, but from the other side. This is the stuff that gets the "A for Effort" and LOL for outcome. But once the laughter dies down, it also inspires a warm feel-good respect for crafters who aren't afraid to fail. After all, even if there's not a mortal alive except Martha who can make a Waxed Heart worthy of hanging in your window to catch the sun, why shouldn't many try? When it goes wrong, why shouldn't the rest of us enjoy this Epic Fail? And then look at all the full-color photos that document it.
Home decor fails, fashion fails, holiday fails, food fails, kid crafting fails-- as one anonymous crafter said: "It wasn't supposed to end this way." Luckily for us, it did."�
